course: dictionary
lesson: 7230
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The word physical is a good example. «We do physical education every Tuesday» means the lesson is about moving your body. In a science lesson, a physical change is different: it changes the shape of something, but not what it is made of.
explain: To work out which meaning is meant, use the context clues. Ask: what is the subject? Is the sentence about a body, a shape, a rock or a river? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: Physical can also mean real and solid, things you can touch and see. In geography, mountains and rivers are called physical features. The word is about the body or about the real, solid world, not about thoughts or feelings.
fact: Physical means about the body, not the mind: «physical exercise» and «physical pain» are about your body.
fact: Physical can also mean real and solid, things you can touch and see.
fact: In science, «folding, bending and cutting» are physical changes: they change only the shape, not what the material is.
fact: A physical change, like melting ice, can be undone, and it makes no new substance.
fact: In American English, «a physical» is a check-up of your body by a doctor.
exercise: «We do physical education every Tuesday.» In this sentence, physical is about | the weather | *the body and moving | the colour of the walls | the mind and thinking
exercise: Melting ice is a physical change, so which statement is true? | It is a chemical change | It makes a new substance | *It can be undone and makes no new substance
exercise: «The mountains and rivers are physical features of the land.» What does physical mean here? | About the mind | Very quiet | Only found in books | *Real things you can see and touch
test: «Folding, bending and cutting paper are physical changes.» Why are they physical changes? | They turn the paper into a new substance | *They change only the shape, not what the paper is | They can only happen at night | They are chemical changes
test: «He had a physical before the football season.» What is a physical here? | *A check-up of his body by a doctor | A lesson about sport | A type of football boot | A very loud whistle
exam: «The doctor said the pain was physical, not in his mind.» What does physical mean here? | Very loud | Made of paper | *About the body | About the mind
